185: fixed-star normal product alone is not that missing map.
186: 
187: This working note is not exported as a theorem. It does not
188: alter the exact source-zero \(C_2\) comparison of K60, whose
189: same scalar test gives zero \(C_2\) right coordinate.
190: 
191: ## SCN.5. The actual outer normal marking omitted by K25
192: 
193: The preceding SCN.4 sentence saying that the missing map has not
194: been identified is retained as the earlier stage of this audit.
195: The following calculation now identifies an explicit outer
196: normal-line mismatch. The pre-addition file is retained under
197: records/attempts/scalar_c1_before_outer_marking.
198: 
199: Keep every unit of SCN.1. The native fixed-curve \(C_0\) charts
200: have first base \(b\), normal pair \((a,c)\), and second base
201: \(\kappa w\), normal pair
202: \[
203:              \bigl(\alpha v,(\kappa\alpha)^{-1}u\bigr).
204:                                                         \tag{SCN.15}
205: \]
206: The negative physical weight is the first normal coordinate
207: in both ordered pairs. In the actual \(C_1\) native chart
208: \((z,n_0,n_1)=(c,a,b)\), the fixed branch is
209: \(z=n_0=0\), with base \(n_1=b\) and normal pair \((a,c)\).
210: Thus its first endpoint agrees literally with (SCN.15).
211: 
212: In its second chart
213: \[
214:               (z',n'_0,n'_1)
215:                    =(\eta v,g w,(g\eta)^{-1}u),
216: \]
217: the fixed branch is \(z'=n'_1=0\), with base \(n'_0=g w\)
218: and ordered negative/positive normal pair
219: \[
220:                     \bigl(\eta v,(g\eta)^{-1}u\bigr).
221:                                                         \tag{SCN.16}
222: \]
223: Consequently the actual coordinate map from the native
224: \(C_0\) normal pair to this \(C_1\) pair at the second branch
225: has base factor \(g/\kappa\) and normal matrix
226: \[
227:        R=\operatorname{diag}
228:           \left(\frac{\eta}{\alpha},
229:                        \frac{\kappa\alpha}{g\eta}\right).
230:                                                         \tag{SCN.17}
231: \]
232: This is an equality of the displayed coordinates, with no
233: change of period or omission of a bounded multiplier.
234: The first branch has the identity normal matrix.
235: 
236: Divide (SCN.17) by its reference value at \(\lambda_*\).
237: The units \(\kappa,\alpha,g,\beta\) are independent of the
238: scalar parameter. Hence on the positive fixed-radius loop,
239: \[
240:         R R_*^{-1}
241:            =\operatorname{diag}(e^{i\theta},e^{-i\theta}).
242:                                                         \tag{SCN.18}
243: \]
244: The physical positive-weight complex normal structure
245: conjugates the first coordinate. Thus the actual Hopf
246: spinor coordinate map in (SCN.18) is
247: \[
248:                          e^{-i\theta}I_2.             \tag{SCN.19}
249: \]
250: At the other endpoint it is \(I_2\). Its determinant winds
251: \(-2\) at the second endpoint and \(0\) at the first.
252: For \(\lambda=r^m\) these windings are \(-2m\) and \(0\).
253: They have been calculated from the actual arrows, not
254: selected from SCN.14 or from a desired flop sign.
255: 
256: K25.7 and K25.8 compare the two *inner* charged-cap maps.
257: Their identical physical-circle gauge can be removed
258: there by one cap frame. Equations (SCN.15)--(SCN.19)
259: compare those native master charts to the two *outer*
260: fixed-curve caps. They give different endpoint gauges.
261: Multiplying both by a common parameter scalar leaves
262: their ratio \(e^{-i\theta}\) unchanged. Therefore the
263: inner common-gauge calculation alone does not establish
264: the claimed pullback of the outer normal-sphere line.
265: The precise unsupported sentence is K25's assertion,
266: after identifying the four fixed-boundary charges,
267: that its parameter circle is a separate factor and
268: consequently \(b^2=0\).
269: 
270: ## SCN.6. The integral Cech class with an explicit orientation
271: 
272: Here is the line class of the actual mismatch, separately
273: from the orientation of the full characteristic bordism.
274: Let a spatial circle be the union of a master interval
275: from endpoint \(0\) to endpoint \(1\) and a cap interval
276: traversed from endpoint \(1\) back to endpoint \(0\).
277: Orient its parameter circle by increasing \(\theta\).
278: Use the coordinate arrows from the master frame to the
279: cap frame
280: \[
281:         y_{\rm cap}=g_j(\theta)y_{\rm master},\qquad
282:                  g_0=1,\quad g_1=e^{-im\theta}.
283:                                                         \tag{SCN.20}
284: \]
285: These are (SCN.19), with the indicated arrow and ordering.
286: They determine a line \(L_m\) on the resulting two-torus.
287: In this explicitly prescribed spatial orientation,
288: \[
289:        \langle c_1(L_m),[S^1_{\rm spatial}
290:                               \times S^1_\theta]\rangle=-m.
291:                                                         \tag{SCN.21}
292: \]
293: One direct verification keeps the connection arrow.
294: Set \(A_{\rm master}=0\). For the convention
295: \(\nabla=d+A\), equation (SCN.20) forces
296: \(A_{\rm cap}=-dg_j\,g_j^{-1}\), hence \(0\) at endpoint
297: \(0\) and \(im\,d\theta\) at endpoint \(1\).
298: Parametrize the cap in the temporary direction \(0\to1\)
299: and interpolate with \(A_{\rm cap}=im\rho(s)d\theta\),
300: where \(\rho\) is constant \(0\) and \(1\) on the
301: respective collars. Its curvature integral in that
302: temporary direction is \(m\). The oriented spatial
303: circle traverses the cap in the opposite direction,
304: giving (SCN.21). This also gives the integral Cech
305: calculation without differentiating a multivalued log.
306: The positive Hopf normal two-plane has the scalar
307: transition (SCN.20) on both summands; its determinant
308: crossing class is therefore \(2c_1(L_m)\), with
309: evaluation \(-2m\).
310: 
311: This calculation identifies a nonzero relative line
312: class and fixes its sign in the displayed two-torus
313: orientation. We have not yet identified that oriented
314: two-torus with the oriented four-dimensional fixed
315: base in K25's full bordism, nor computed its sphere
316: class or the resulting value of \(b^2\). No numerical
317: characteristic correction is assigned by SCN.21.
318: 
319: ## SCN.7. The simultaneous-product premise also fails directly
320: 
321: Apply the complete determinant square PO.5--PO.11
322: of K47 to the actual scalar charts (SCN.4), retaining
323: their labelled vertices and all three labelled curves.
324: The pointed \(C_2\) and \(C_1\) products force
325: \[
326:                  a_*+u_*=0,\qquad c_*+v_*=m.
327: \]
328: The arbitrary invertible positive-weight complex
329: normal derivative along \(C_0\) forces
330: \[
331:       (-v_*+u_*)+\operatorname{wind}\kappa
332:             +2\operatorname{wind}\alpha-(-a_*+c_*)=0.
333: \]
334: Substitution yields
335: \(\operatorname{wind}\kappa+2\operatorname{wind}\alpha
336:  -\operatorname{wind}\eta=-m=0\), which is impossible
337: for \(m\ne0\). The argument allows full off-diagonal
338: \(GL_2(\mathbb C)\) normal matrices; it does not assume
339: diagonality away from the vertices. Thus the actual
340: marked delta-equivariant simultaneous plumbing product
341: asserted in K29 Section 3 does not exist for this
342: positive scalar loop. The separate native \(C_1\)
343: product of SCN.6--SCN.9 and the ordinary quaternion
344: product are not excluded by this determinant square.
345: 
346: The exact local maps and integral mismatch are recorded
347: by code/part3/scalar_c1_outer_marking.py and its output.
348: The dependency notice is kept separately in
349: notes/part3_scalar_consistency_dependencies.md.
350: 
351: ## SCN.8. The complete native C2 comparison
352: 
353: The diagonal \(C_2\) star in these same seam-closed
354: charts has the actual coordinates
355: \[
356:         (z,n_0,n_1)=(a,b,c),\qquad
357:         (z',n'_0,n'_1)=(u,v,w).
358: \]
359: Its full transition is
360: \[
361:        (u,v,w)=(a^{-1},ab,ac),\qquad
362:                  z'=z^{-1},\quad n'_i=zn_i.           \tag{SCN.22}
363: \]
364: There is no omitted unit or parameter factor in this
365: transition. The seam (SCN.4) acts on its first chart by
366: \[
367:        (z,n_0,n_1)\longmapsto
368:                     ((AD)^{-1}z,An_0,Dn_1)
369: \]
370: and on the second by
371: \((z',n'_0,n'_1)\mapsto(ADz',D^{-1}n'_0,A^{-1}n'_1)\).
372: With \(z=a_1/a_0,\ n_i=a_0c_i\), its full Cox lift is
373: \[
374:    (a_0,a_1,c_0,c_1)\longmapsto
375:                 (a_0,(AD)^{-1}a_1,Ac_0,Dc_1).        \tag{SCN.23}
376: \]
377: It preserves \(q=a_0a_1c_0c_1\), the auxiliary action,
378: the physical circle and every actual period translate.
379: It extends over both small resolutions and has the
380: displayed inverse at the same \(q\).
381: 
382: For two primitive scalar turns, SCN.11 and the actual
383: prisms DZ.19, with \(w_2=-1,w_0=0\), give
384: \[
385:                     V_{22}=2,\qquad \delta_2=2.
386: \]
387: The local ambient-to-product frame comparison therefore
388: gives the ordinary relative pair \((-2,0)\).
389: The native-to-ordinary boundary map is literally
390: \[
391:                 q_H\longmapsto
392:                  (UH_1U^{-1})q_HH_1.                 \tag{SCN.24}
393: \]
394: Its left degree is \(+2\) and its right degree is zero.
395: The inverse extends by the explicit cylinder retraction
396: of OR.2, with endpoint \(L^{-2}\); its coefficient maps
397: extend over \(D^3\times D^4\). Thus the native doubled
398: pair is \((0,0)\).
399: 
400: Equations (SCN.5), (SCN.22) and (SCN.23) are the literal
401: pullback of one native \(C_2\) product. Consequently
402: the doubled relative return is its actual square.
403: The free coordinates of its single relative return
404: are \((0,0)\), since multiplication by two is injective
405: on these two integral coordinates. The actual
406: single-star Cox conjugation changes the central
407: seven-sphere class by its right integer, which is
408: zero. This establishes equality of the initial and
409: reflected scalar return classes without division in
410: \(\Theta_7\).
411: 
412: The same maps retain every integral scalar winding
413: \(J\). On the double pullback use
414: \[
415:        t=J,\quad l=(2J,0,2J),\quad
416:        I=(-2J,2J,-2J),\quad W=(2J,0,0).
417:                                                         \tag{SCN.25}
418: \]
419: The ordinary \(C_2\) pair is \((-2J,0)\), its native
420: pair is \((0,0)\), and the single native pair is
421: again \((0,0)\). This includes negative winding and
422: zero winding, with the same physical circle.
423: 
424: For the canonical cap families the ordinary closing
425: may be \(q^e\) with either sign of \(e\), rather than
426: the primitive cap-to-ordinary \(q^{-1}\) of SCN.1.
427: The exact reindexing is then \(B^{-e}\), and its
428: bounded map is
429: \((Z,V)\mapsto(g^{-e}Z,\eta^{-e}V)\).
430: Use the cut seam
431: \[
432:        (Z,V)\mapsto
433:          \bigl(e^{e\chi\log g}Z,e^{e\chi\log\eta}V\bigr).
434:                                                         \tag{SCN.26}
435: \]
436: It obeys \(C_{\rm end}E=1\) with all derivatives.
437: Its double is still the literal pullback (SCN.5).
438: Thus the full source and cap closing squares already
439: proved in K26/K28/K32 are carried unchanged; no norm
440: sign is reversed. Parameter-independent bounded
441: closing units are carried through their fixed
442: logarithms. The unit winding in the actual period
443: matrix is still \((0,0;0,J)\), so (SCN.25) applies.
444: The scalar equality needed by K58 for its initial
445: and reflected fans follows from these actual maps.
446: 
447: ## SCN.9. The C2 characteristic bordism has no outer mismatch
448: 
449: There is also a direct narrow repair of the integer
450: characteristic comparison. At the first fixed branch
451: of the \(C_2\) native star, its fixed base and normal
452: pair are exactly \(b\) and \((a,c)\). At the second,
453: they are \(w\) and \((v,u)\). Relative to the native
454: \(C_0\) coordinates (SCN.15), the second arrow is
455: \[
456:  \text{base factor }\kappa^{-1},\qquad
457:  \text{normal matrix }\operatorname{diag}
458:                            (\alpha^{-1},\kappa\alpha).
459:                                                         \tag{SCN.27}
460: \]
461: Both this map and its first-branch identity are
462: independent of the scalar parameter. After carrying
463: their fixed logarithms, the outer normal maps are
464: constant in that parameter.
465: 
466: In the \(C_2\) Cox coordinates of (SCN.23), the
467: parameter factor has physical weights
468: \((0,-1,0,+1)\). The two inner charged boundary maps
469: therefore have one identical scalar gauge, as in
470: the actual master and joint-cap maps of K17.
